{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971793-incorporating-famous-lost-cities-into-mage","id":971793,"title":"Incorporating famous lost cities into Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-17T23:39:23-07:00","id":971793,"title":"Incorporating famous lost cities into Mage","content":"One of my favorite classic Fortean topics is the subject of lost cities, islands, and continents, and I think they fit in Mage quite well. My idea for Lemuria comes from my remake project: it was an attempt to rebuild or recreate Atlantis that went horribly wrong. Now the island floats in a spatially-dubious zone of the ocean that sensors and satellites can't pick up, strewn with ruins and wreckage and danger. It's ringed by smaller islands, home to small communities of Awakened/Hollows and other supernatural creatures. <br /> <br /> Magonia is a massive invisible airship the size of an island constructed by the Diamond during the Middle Ages, which still sails the skies to this day. <br /> <br /> I'm stuck on a good idea for Agartha, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T00:03:12-07:00","id":971798,"title":"","content":"I think Secrets of the Shattered Temple delves briefly into Shangri-La somewhere, and Mummy covered both Irem and Ubar somewhat. If that whole Post-Roman Britain setting ever happens, it'll probably touch on Hy-Brasil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T00:52:12-07:00","id":971813,"title":"","content":"Worth mentioning thing is that 2E has a lot of different 'Atlantis', because each one is a different mythical community of magicians. My private theory says that each reflects the history of 'First Atlantis', leading to a repeated cycle of Golden Age and the Fall, in each of those societies. This is reflected also on the history of magicians, where legends go on the same tropes. And finally Darshanas cults from <i>To the Strongest</i> Dark Era make sense when each one reflects the 'Caste' originating in community of 'First-Atlantis-That-Never-Was'. Basically, Time Before is hodgepodge of diffrent societies and civilizations that reflect common themes set by 'First Atlantis'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971793-incorporating-famous-lost-cities-into-mage?p=971798#post971798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that whole Post-Roman Britain setting ever happens, it'll probably touch on Hy-Brasil.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Camelot, as local name for Ruins of Time Before in Britain, according to <b>DaveB</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971793-incorporating-famous-lost-cities-into-mage?p=971798#post971798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Secrets of the Shattered Temple</div> </div> </div> </div>Secrets of the <i>Ruined</i> Temple","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-18-2016, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T01:35:45-07:00","id":971834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971793-incorporating-famous-lost-cities-into-mage#post971793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my favorite classic Fortean topics is the subject of lost cities, islands, and continents, and I think they fit in Mage quite well. My idea for Lemuria comes from my remake project: it was an attempt to rebuild or recreate Atlantis that went horribly wrong. Now the island floats in a spatially-dubious zone of the ocean that sensors and satellites can't pick up, strewn with ruins and wreckage and danger. It's ringed by smaller islands, home to small communities of Awakened/Hollows and other supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> Magonia is a massive invisible airship the size of an island constructed by the Diamond during the Middle Ages, which still sails the skies to this day.<br /> <br /> I'm stuck on a good idea for Agartha, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is baseline for 2e. Check out the Ruined Temple book1e. It covers your questions. 2e clarifies it enough so that it's a moot point.\u200b The Exarchs tried to hide the time before but there are all sorts of lost sites that make no sense given the the current timeline. Think of Lara Croft as as Mysterious sleepwalker. Now.think what sleepwalkers the other orders employ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 09-18-2016, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T22:22:32-07:00","id":990275,"title":"","content":"What are some good Mysteries that could bring a Cabal to Lemuria? One of the most obvious ones is &quot;figure out what went wrong&quot;- I'd like to have it be ambiguous how exactly it went pear-shaped, and leave it up to the ST to decide. The answer could have some pretty major implications: &quot;the Seers sabotaged it&quot; implies, for example, that the idea of trying build a new Atlantis is fundamentally sound but was taken down by outside forces, while &quot;it's creators destroyed it in their own hubris&quot; is an entirely different takeaway, one that works better if the theme you're going for is &quot;don't hold on to the past&quot; or &quot;pining for a lost golden age achieves nothing&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T23:22:15-07:00","id":990294,"title":"","content":"We need to know more about Lemuria you talk about - what sources, what period, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T23:26:31-07:00","id":990295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971793-incorporating-famous-lost-cities-into-mage#post971793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My idea for Lemuria comes from my remake project: it was an attempt to rebuild or recreate Atlantis that went horribly wrong. Now the island floats in a spatially-dubious zone of the ocean that sensors and satellites can't pick up, strewn with ruins and wreckage and danger. It's ringed by smaller islands, home to small communities of Awakened/Hollows and other supernatural creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds kind of like an above-water Rapture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971793-incorporating-famous-lost-cities-into-mage#post971793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magonia is a massive invisible airship the size of an island constructed by the Diamond during the Middle Ages, which still sails the skies to this day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just like Columbia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971793-incorporating-famous-lost-cities-into-mage#post971793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm stuck on a good idea for Agartha, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not roll with the parallels and model it after Citidel Station?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T23:34:36-07:00","id":990298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971793-incorporating-famous-lost-cities-into-mage?p=990275#post990275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are some good Mysteries that could bring a Cabal to Lemuria? One of the most obvious ones is &amp;quot;figure out what went wrong&amp;quot;- I'd like to have it be ambiguous how exactly it went pear-shaped, and leave it up to the ST to decide. The answer could have some pretty major implications: &amp;quot;the Seers sabotaged it&amp;quot; implies, for example, that the idea of trying build a new Atlantis is fundamentally sound but was taken down by outside forces, while &amp;quot;it's creators destroyed it in their own hubris&amp;quot; is an entirely different takeaway, one that works better if the theme you're going for is &amp;quot;don't hold on to the past&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;pining for a lost golden age achieves nothing&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they invented special serums that could alter the DNA of Sleepers to turn them into Proximi, each one granting them access to a different Blessing. And then they found a way to distill Supernal gnosis into like an injectible serum that grants Arcane Beats so Proximi could expand their capacity for Blessings. After a while, the whole city could have fallen to anarchy as the Proximi warred with each other for access to the precious Mana and Arcane Beat formula they need to fuel their Blessings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T23:51:06-07:00","id":990304,"title":"","content":"Hm, remember the False Awakening from The Unbidden? That could be related, in terms of &quot;unstable forced-awakenings&quot;. <br /> <br /> To add to that scenario, maybe the various Awakensd leaders overused the serum, because they started competing to see who could have more Proximus servants, leading to too many fighting over too few resources? And I'd like things to get even worse from there- my idea is that the island itself is now an incredibly dangerous unstable magical zone, extremely difficult to navigate, with ever-shifting terrain, not to mention various dangerous magical mutants present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-20-2016, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T00:00:21-07:00","id":990309,"title":"","content":"Consider googling Spirit Science or other New Age youtubers they are a goldmine of plot ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10831-bauran","name":"Bauran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10831_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:30:07-07:00","id":990555,"title":"","content":"Can't speak to what your city should be, but I'm folding in together the idea of the Adytum from the Mysterium book, i.e. Knock-off Atlantis, in with Celtic Mythology and some of the Underworld lore we have. Idea is that it was meant to be the perfect reserve of magical knowledge, and to preserve knowledge perfectly, knowledge cannot die, and, to put it it glibly, that which is already dead cannot die. So the Phoenix Brethren were ancient Celtic mages who crafted a city underneath the West of Ireland, and crafted a permanent opening into the Underworld beneath that would lead to the Aetheneum Dead Domain as described in Book of the Dead. This lets me tie together a few parallels between the myth of the Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann and the Atlantis myth, most notably the associations in both between West and magic, among other things (the main villain in that mythic arc, Balor, even has a glass tower ^_^).<br /> <br /> But of course, something went <i>very </i>wrong. When they actually find it it'll be full on Lovecraft's &quot;The Nameless City&quot;. Lots of twisted monsters, strange writings, cries in the dark. Thinking of good old Sleepers unearthing the soul-starved Preta that were trapped within. Then we can start with a &quot;why is there a sudden spike in cannibalism in this farming village&quot; plot hook when I'm ready to start that off. And of course, there are bigger rumblings in the Underworld. Someone's trying to usurp that connection for their own ends.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the Seers have already found out about it and the Pentacle is on the back foot. They're ready to go to war over it.<br /> <br /> Feel free to steal any of that if it sounds decent or sparks stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","user":"AinSoph","date":". 10-20-2016, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:33:01-07:00","id":990557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971793-incorporating-famous-lost-cities-into-mage?p=990304#post990304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, remember the False Awakening from The Unbidden? That could be related, in terms of &amp;quot;unstable forced-awakenings&amp;quot;. <br /> <br /> To add to that scenario, maybe the various Awakensd leaders overused the serum, because they started competing to see who could have more Proximus servants, leading to too many fighting over two few resources?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I should have been clearer, text medium and all. That wasn't a serious suggestion, it was the plot of Bioshock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:42:00-07:00","id":990563,"title":"","content":"Definitely going to steal AinSoph's idea, but I'd probably have Lemuria as another utopia gone wrong, mostly because I like the whole &quot;island vacation in magic hell&quot; idea. <br /> <br /> And Charlaquin, is it bad that it still sounds like a cool idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T13:44:29-07:00","id":990604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971793-incorporating-famous-lost-cities-into-mage?p=990563#post990563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Charlaquin, is it bad that it still sounds like a cool idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all! Bioshock is awesome and it does the dystopia thing you're looking for extremely well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T13:50:32-07:00","id":990609,"title":"","content":"I still need to play that. <br /> <br /> Part of the setup is that Lemuria is so unstable and dangerous that none of the factions have even been able to establish permanent presences on it or take control of it in any way (whether or not this is possible is up to the ST, but if it is the reason it hasn't been done yet is that no faction has been willing to pledge the resources to see if it's true). There is, however, a ring of islands around it supporting various settlements, and the flying island of Magonia periodically passes by to drop off adventurers. <br /> <br /> The relationship between Lemuria and other splats is another flexible thing, but is assumed to be &quot;weird as hell&quot;. It could be accessible via the Hedge, or it might be completely cut off from it. And of course its Shadow is completely fucked up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:34:40-07:00","id":990635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971793-incorporating-famous-lost-cities-into-mage?p=990609#post990609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still need to play that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, the Collection is out! Comes with 1, 2, Infinite, and Burial at Sea for the price of one game, and it'd be a great source of inspiration for these lost cities of yours. Rapture and Columbia are both complete dystopias of different different natures, and they map pretty well to your cities here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:36:41-07:00","id":990637,"title":"","content":"I have the iOS version, is it worth it to get the collection too? Sorry for getting off topic. <br /> <br /> If Magonia implodes (which is a likely end for most Mage megaprojects) it would basically be &quot;less-racist Columbia&quot;, too.<br /> <br /> Here are some examples of phenomena players could run into in Lemuria, each representing a different arcanum going out of control: <br /> <br /> - A swamp where anything that died instantly rises as a zombie. <br /> - A non-Euclidean cavern of stone arches, each of which teleports anyone who steps through it to somewhere else on the island. <br /> - A rusting, gigantic statue that absorbs mana and can move if it gets enough. <br /> - A forest of animals, separated into warring factions. Each faction makes a prediction for the future and then they fight. The winning faction's prediction comes true. <br /> - A valley where the Shadow and reality are switched. Physical entities that enter it become intangible spirit beings, while ephemeral beings become fully tangible. <br /> - A glade of parasitic plants that use telepathy to lure people to them so they can drain their thoughts. <br /> - Rain that causes anything it gets wet to slow down in time depending on how wet they get. <br /> - An enormous alchemical forge, with a legion of golems that periodically deliver materials to it, which it forges into random items, often explosive. <br /> - Sonically controlled lightning storms whose intensity and targets can be dictated by singing or playing music.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-28-2016, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:45:48-07:00","id":990644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971793-incorporating-famous-lost-cities-into-mage?p=990637#post990637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the iOS version, is it worth it to get the collection too? Sorry for getting off topic. <br /> <br /> If Magonia implodes (which is a likely end for most Mage megaprojects) it would basically be &amp;quot;less-racist Columbia&amp;quot;, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, if you already have them, nah. Not unless you're the sort who's expernce will be made or broken by outdated graphics. Or if you really want the bonus features it comes with. It mostly amounts to an update to HD, which is more significant in 1 and 2 than it is in Infinite. The vending machines are far less obnoxious though, which is a relief. I wish they had overhauled the hacking system though, that pipe minigame was dumb.<br /> <br /> No worries about the off-topic, it's my fault we're on this subject <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:09:29-07:00","id":991976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971793-incorporating-famous-lost-cities-into-mage?p=971813#post971813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth mentioning thing is that 2E has a lot of different 'Atlantis', because each one is a different mythical community of magicians. My private theory says that each reflects the history of 'First Atlantis', leading to a repeated cycle of Golden Age and the Fall, in each of those societies. This is reflected also on the history of magicians, where legends go on the same tropes. And finally Darshanas cults from <i>To the Strongest</i> Dark Era make sense when each one reflects the 'Caste' originating in community of 'First-Atlantis-That-Never-Was'. Basically, Time Before is hodgepodge of diffrent societies and civilizations that reflect common themes set by 'First Atlantis'.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a Dark Eras game, I asked one PC to have a particular concept: she would be a mage from the Time Before, encountered lost in a Ruin of the Time Before.<br /> <br /> The explicit advice I gave her was that every time she tried to think back on the Awakened City, it would be different every time. The nature of its government (city-state? small kingdom? modern democracy over a large area?), the nature of its technology (futuristic? Ultra fantasy?), the nature of its people (human? what color skin?), its architecture (spires? Caves beneath the earth? Maybe dozens of cities or a floating castle.) Her own memories of herself would be shattered and weird. A few things would be consistent, like for instance that she was a soldier, that she fought in a great battle, that she lost - essentially, symbols that nail down certain facts but without consistent details or even a consistent order of events.<br /> <br /> Eventually, this would settle into a fairly stable form, but they would always, forever, be aware that their memories of their original home are <i>wrong.</i> Whatever they settle on is just a false image that their brain has accepted. Only when they Ascend could they ever again see their life as it truly was, whatever that was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T01:53:50-07:00","id":993384,"title":"","content":"I used the myth of Ys in my last Werewolf/Mage campaign (sunkened city of Bretagne in France).<br /> <br /> Basically, the legend says that Gradlon, the king of Cornwall (Cornouailles), as a beloved daughter named Dahu/A\u00e8s (confused naming). For his daughter, he build a white city on the sea, whose walls and dams keep waters away. But Dahu/A\u00e8s was a sinful woman, who turn Ys the White in a city of lust (christian retcon). So the devil seduced her, took the keys from her and opened the gates, letting the sea flooding Ys.<br /> <br /> In my setting, King Gradlon had two daughters, Dahu and A\u00e8s, and he built a city for each. Ys the White for Dahu on the sea, and Kar-A\u00e8s (actual french city of Carhaix) for A\u00e8s on the land. The two awakened, and went at war against each other. During the war, A\u00e8s destroyed Ys by pushing it in the Abyss, cursing Dahu to never die until she loose her life on Ys ground, effectively granting her a sad immortality. After that the campaign revolved around an Idigam who wanted to acess the Abyss to do mischieving things (long story short), using Ys as a gigantic gateway between the Flesh and the deep Abyss. Dahu was an hidden mage NPC, pretending to just be a relic merchant and lore specialist, who gain the PC affection along the chronicle. She finally died in the PC arms in the final scene which confront them to the idigam in Ys itself, after diving head on in the Abyss. Quite epic ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3883,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","user":"Arabidopsis","date":". 10-26-2016, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T02:03:50-07:00","id":993387,"title":"","content":"I've known siblings like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}